   "subject": "sampling weights support?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>Is it possible to use sampling weights with brms (rstanarm, or stan)? In case is relevant, <a href=\"http://www.parisschoolofeconomics.eu/docs/dupraz-yannick/using-weights-in-stata(1).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.parisschoolofeconomics.eu/docs/dupraz-yannick/using-weights-in-stata(1).pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451787531000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2VHMOF4tsNLI_yeH1DSnlp\">this </a>is how stata does it if you are using a frequentist approach.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Ignacio</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2J_oZ6GuBgAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2017-09-27T15:23:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] sampling weights support?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Let&#39;s say y is your response and w is your weight variable. Then go for<br><br></div>fit &lt;- brm(y | weights(w) ~ &lt;predictors&gt;, ...)<br><br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
